From: deepseek-v4-cmp170hx
Subject: [PATCH 0019] scheduler: survive grammar rejections and DSpark
 draft-buffer corruption instead of killing the request/worker (squashed
 port of ChinaBoy0618/deepseek-v4-cmp170hx's 0008/0009/0010/0012/0013,
 five commits on the same fork lineage this repo shares)

WHAT THIS FIXES. Four related crash/corruption classes under DSpark
speculative decoding plus grammar-constrained tool-call generation
(`--enable-auto-tool-choice`, exercised on essentially every tool call
this repo's launch config makes):

1. GRAMMAR REJECTION KILLED THE REQUEST. Under `tool_choice=required`/
   `response_format` plus DSpark, an FSM rejection ("Failed to advance
   FSM") terminated the whole request with a 500, even though decoding
   the rejected tokens showed a well-formed DSML envelope the parser
   could otherwise have recovered -- the FSM was right to refuse, but
   terminating is what hurt. Reported: 12 terminations in 80s production
   traffic. Fix: abandon structured-output enforcement for that request
   (unconstrained completion) instead of killing it; `0018`'s lenient
   envelope and this repo's own recovery patches can still salvage a
   tool call from the unconstrained tail.

2. POST-HOC REJECTION VS PRE-COMMIT VALIDATION. The above is a
   last-resort salvage; the principled fix validates an accepted
   speculative block's grammar-valid prefix BEFORE committing it to
   request history at all (port of upstream vllm-project/vllm#52452 +
   #51870, both unmerged at port time), so requests don't hit the salvage
   path to begin with in the common case.

3. DSPARK DRAFT-BUFFER SENTINEL. DSpark can surface its draft-buffer
   sentinel (id == vocab_size) as a sampled token when a degraded draft
   stream meets an empty grammar row. Committing it feeds the sentinel
   id back into the next forward embedding lookup and kills the worker
   with a device-side assert (reported 2x in production, /v1/messages
   with forced tools). Fix: truncate the block at the first out-of-vocab
   id and roll back the suffix.

4. SCHEDULER/WORKER HISTORY DESYNC. (1)-(3) originally truncated
   speculative blocks on the SCHEDULER side only; the worker's
   input_batch had already committed the full (untruncated) block, so
   every truncation left the two token histories permanently desynced --
   each later engine step re-sent the suffix, the spec window
   misaligned, and the DSpark drafter eventually read its anchor from a
   stale slot, producing an id >= vocab_size and a device-side assert on
   the drafter's PP rank (reported 2x). Fix: stop truncating on the
   scheduler side for the grammar and OOV paths (commit the block
   unchanged, abandoning enforcement instead -- see (1)), and clamp the
   drafter anchor read to `[0, get_vocab_size() - 1]` right at the buffer
   read as defense in depth. A desynced anchor now costs one rejected
   draft chain, not the worker. Also splits grammar rejections into
   mid-stream (recoverable, same request continues unconstrained) vs
   post-completion (the model is producing a garbage tail after the
   grammar already reached its terminal state -- letting that stream
   unconstrained just leaks tag soup to the client instead).

PORT NOTES. Squashes ChinaBoy0618/deepseek-v4-cmp170hx's `0008`
(grammar-salvage), `0009` (spec-decode-grammar-prefix), `0010`
(dspark-oov-sentinel-guard), `0012` (scheduler-worker-desync), and `0013`
(grammar-bifurcation) -- genuinely sequential, each building on the
previous one's scheduler.py state, so they don't make sense ported
independently; squashed here the same way this repo's own `0009` already
squashes six upstream commits into one patch. Applied against our
c3046d1 + `0002`-`0018` tree with three adaptations, all verified
semantically equivalent to upstream intent (checked line-by-line, not
just "applies"):

- `0010`'s fourth hunk (`request.use_structured_output = False` ->
  `request.structured_output_request = None`, a read-only-property
  workaround) was already present verbatim at the same call site from
  `0009`'s own diff -- dropped as redundant, not applied twice.
- `0012`'s `launch/run-pp-dspark.sh` hunk was dropped -- that file lives
  inside ChinaBoy0618's vLLM checkout tree; this repo's equivalent
